Dear colleagues

From today, we are Stonegrove University.

The name on the gate has changed, and so has everything that carries it: the =
website, the prospectus, the signage, the templates you will find in Communic=
ations / Brand on the Hub. One logo, one palette, two typefaces, one way of w=
riting. A short guide explains it all and I would love it if you read it; it =
takes ten minutes.

Why. Because we are one institution. Elves and Dwarves, five faculties, fifty=
-five programmes, and until today, five letterheads. The College of the Vale =
was a fine name for what we were. Stonegrove University is the name for what =
we are.

What this means for you. Use the new templates from today. Retire the old one=
s, wherever you have them. Use the new name, and the new names for faculties =
and departments, which are in the guide. If you need anything made, ask Commu=
nications; please do not make it yourself. If you are not sure, ask.

Gentle reminder: the old crest, the old wordmark and the old names belong to =
our history now. We will treat them with respect and we will not use them.

Thank you to everyone on the project board and to Sorell Inkthread, who wrote=
 the guide and designed the logo and will, I suspect, be keeping a close eye =
on all of us.

One voice.

Rhialla

